    {
      "id": 34035,
      "nameEs": "Beatmania IIDX 9th style",
      "originalName": "Beatmania IIDX 9th style",
      "year": 2003,
      "igdbId": 81505,
      "popularity": 0,
      "iconic": false,
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "name_es",
          "value": "Beatmania IIDX 9th style",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "Beatmania IIDX 9th style",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Beatmania IIDX 9th style is one of the many titles in Konami's IIDX rhythm game series, featuring more than 80 tracks, primarily from the arcade version of the same title. As usual for the beatmania series, the player is given seven piano keys and a turntable, and must play along with the notes that scroll down the screen to play the music. 9th style features a completely revamped interface compared to the previous titles, owing to the more powerful hardware that the arcade version ran on.\n\nThere are three main modes: Arcade mode tasks the player with completing several tracks in succession, Free mode lets the player freely play any unlocked song, and Training mode lets the player practice parts of songs without danger of failure. The Beginner's mode from 5th style and the Class mode from 7th style are also present, as is the gallery mode.",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "beatmania IIDX 9th style es uno de los muchos títulos de la serie de juegos de ritmo IIDX de Konami, con más de 80 canciones, principalmente de la versión recreativa del mismo título. Como es habitual en la serie beatmania, el jugador dispone de siete teclas de piano y un plato, y debe seguir las notas que bajan por la pantalla para tocar la música. 9th style tiene una interfaz completamente renovada respecto a los títulos anteriores, gracias al hardware más potente en el que funcionaba la versión recreativa.\n\nHay tres modos principales: el modo Arcade exige completar varias canciones seguidas, el modo Free permite tocar libremente cualquier canción desbloqueada y el modo Training permite practicar partes de las canciones sin riesgo de fallar. También están presentes el modo Beginner de 5th style, el modo Class de 7th style y el modo galería.",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "2003",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
